### =========================================================================
### 🎓 REFRESH TOKENS — dalawang token
### 📅 Day 51 · Phase 11 (Mas ligtas na sessions)
### =========================================================================
### access token  (cookie `token`)         = JWT, 15 MINUTO, hindi naka-save sa database
### refresh token (cookie `refresh_token`) = random, 7 ARAW, SHA-256 hash lang ang nasa `refresh_tokens`
###                                           Path=/api/auth → ipinapadala LANG sa /api/auth/*
###
### Kapag expired ang access token → 401 → POST /api/auth/refresh → bagong access token → ulitin.
### (Ginagawa ito ng frontend nang kusa — api/auth.ts, apiFetch.)
###
### Code: backend/src/lib/session.ts · backend/src/routes/auth.ts (/auth/refresh)
### Test: backend/src/routes/refresh.test.ts · Diagram: docs/diagrams/06-auth-sequence.md (REFRESH)
### =========================================================================

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 0. Account (isang beses lang — 409 kung mayroon na)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "refresh-demo@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1. Login. Ang inaasahan — DALAWANG Set-Cookie sa headers:
###    token=eyJ...;         Max-Age=900     (15 minuto)   Path=/
###    refresh_token=...;    Max-Age=604800  (7 araw)      Path=/api/auth
### 🔍 Sa database (npm run db:studio → refresh_tokens): ang token_hash ay HINDI kapareho ng
###    refresh_token sa cookie — hash lang ang naka-save
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "refresh-demo@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2. Bagong access token. Ang inaasahan:
###    204 · Set-Cookie: token=<BAGONG JWT>; Max-Age=900
###    (Ipinapadala ng REST Client ang refresh_token cookie dahil /api/auth ang path)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/refresh

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 3. /me gamit ang bagong access token. Ang inaasahan: 200 { "user": { ... } }
GET http://localhost:3000/api/auth/me

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 4. Pekeng refresh token. Ang inaasahan:
###    401 { "error": "Not authenticated" } — at binubura ang dalawang cookie (Expires=1970)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/refresh
Cookie: refresh_token=gawa-gawa-lang

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 5. Mag-login ulit (binura ng #4 ang cookies), tapos logout. Ang inaasahan: 204 — binura ang DALAWANG cookie
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "refresh-demo@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/logout

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 6. Refresh pagkatapos mag-logout. Ang inaasahan: 401 — walang cookie na maipapadala
### ⚠️ Pero AKTIBO pa ang refresh token sa DATABASE (revoked_at = null) — kung may nakakopya nito,
###    gagana pa (tingnan sa db:studio). Aayusin sa Day 53 (totoong logout)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/refresh
